findings.solution:
Do not use unsanitized external input as a URL target. If proxying is required, enforce a strict allowlist of schemes, hosts and ports, validate and normalize the target URL, and preserve/forward the original requestor identity. For example, reject non-http(s) schemes and check target against an allowlist before opening:
    from urllib.parse import urlparse
    allowed = {'https://api.example.com'}
    parsed = urlparse(target)
    if parsed.scheme not in ('http','https') or f'{parsed.scheme}://{parsed.netloc}' not in allowed:
        raise ValueError('Disallowed target')
    return urllib.request.urlopen(target).read()
